<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade-May 24.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade-May 24.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended May 24</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   300	   0.54     646300  193.89    9.39</p>
<p>L &amp; T		  210	   0.37     186800   39.23    9.19</p>
<p>Colgate		300	   0.51     128550   38.57    8.86</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   845	   1.49	43450   36.72    9.19</p>
<p>Sterlite	     270	   0.51     131700   35.56    9.85</p>
<p>ACC		   1110	   2.02	25330   28.12    9.49</p>
<p>MTNL		   275	   0.49	93800   25.80    9.29</p>
<p>BSES		   225	   0.40     107400   24.17    9.27</p>
<p>Cadbury		290	   0.58	68500   19.87   10.43</p>
<p>Dr. Reddy	    210	   0.37	92900   19.51    9.19</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 10.10 percent on an annualised basis against  8.32 % in the previous carry forward account ended May 17</p>
